#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:3
msgid "`nix-shell` - start an interactive shell based on a Nix expression"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-shell` \\[`--arg` _name_ _value_\\] \\[`--argstr` _name_ _value_\\] "
"\\[{`--attr` | `-A`} _attrPath_\\] \\[`--command` _cmd_\\] \\[`--run` "
"_cmd_\\] \\[`--exclude` _regexp_\\] \\[`--pure`\\] \\[`--keep` _name_\\] "
"{{`--packages` | `-p`} {_packages_ | _expressions_} … | \\[_path_\\]}"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:18
msgid "Disambiguation"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:20
msgid ""
"This man page describes the command `nix-shell`, which is distinct from `nix "
"shell`. For documentation on the latter, run `nix shell --help` or see `man "
"nix3-env-shell`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:24
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:26
msgid ""
"The command `nix-shell` will build the dependencies of the specified "
"derivation, but not the derivation itself. It will then start an interactive "
"shell in which all environment variables defined by the derivation _path_ "
"have been set to their corresponding values, and the script `$stdenv/setup` "
"has been sourced. This is useful for reproducing the environment of a "
"derivation for development."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:33
msgid ""
"If _path_ is not given, `nix-shell` defaults to `shell.nix` if it exists, "
"and `default.nix` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:36
msgid ""
"If _path_ starts with `http://` or `https://`, it is interpreted as the URL "
"of a tarball that will be downloaded and unpacked to a temporary location. "
"The tarball must include a single top-level directory containing at least a "
"file named `default.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:41
msgid ""
"If the derivation defines the variable `shellHook`, it will be run after "
"`$stdenv/setup` has been sourced. Since this hook is not executed by regular "
"Nix builds, it allows you to perform initialisation specific to `nix-shell`. "
"For example, the derivation attribute"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:46
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"shellHook =\n"
"  ''\n"
"    echo \"Hello shell\"\n"
"    export SOME_API_TOKEN=\"$(cat ~/.config/some-app/api-token)\"\n"
"  '';\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:54
msgid ""
"will cause `nix-shell` to print `Hello shell` and set the `SOME_API_TOKEN` "
"environment variable to a user-configured value."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:57
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:59
msgid ""
"All options not listed here are passed to `nix-store --realise`, except for "
"`--arg` and `--attr` / `-A` which are passed to `nix-instantiate`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:63
msgid "`--command` _cmd_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:65
msgid ""
"In the environment of the derivation, run the shell command _cmd_. This "
"command is executed in an interactive shell. (Use `--run` to use a non-"
"interactive shell instead.) However, a call to `exit` is implicitly added to "
"the command, so the shell will exit after running the command. To prevent "
"this, add `return` at the end; e.g.  `--command \"echo Hello; return\"` will "
"print `Hello` and then drop you into the interactive shell. This can be "
"useful for doing any additional initialisation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:74
msgid "`--run` _cmd_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:76
msgid ""
"Like `--command`, but executes the command in a non-interactive shell. This "
"means (among other things) that if you hit Ctrl-C while the command is "
"running, the shell exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:80
msgid "`--exclude` _regexp_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:82
msgid ""
"Do not build any dependencies whose store path matches the regular "
"expression _regexp_. This option may be specified multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:85
msgid "`--pure`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:87
msgid ""
"If this flag is specified, the environment is almost entirely cleared before "
"the interactive shell is started, so you get an environment that more "
"closely corresponds to the “real” Nix build. A few variables, in particular "
"`HOME`, `USER` and `DISPLAY`, are retained.  Note that the shell used to run "
"commands is obtained from [`NIX_BUILD_SHELL`](#env-NIX_BUILD_SHELL) / "
"`<nixpkgs>` from `NIX_PATH`, and therefore not affected by `--pure`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:95
msgid "`--packages` / `-p` _packages_…"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:97
msgid ""
"Set up an environment in which the specified packages are present. The "
"command line arguments are interpreted as attribute names inside the Nix "
"Packages collection. Thus, `nix-shell --packages libjpeg openjdk` will start "
"a shell in which the packages denoted by the attribute names `libjpeg` and "
"`openjdk` are present."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:103
msgid "`-i` _interpreter_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:105
msgid ""
"The chained script interpreter to be invoked by `nix-shell`. Only applicable "
"in `#!`\\-scripts (described below)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:108
msgid "`--keep` _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:110
msgid ""
"When a `--pure` shell is started, keep the listed environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:117
msgid "Common Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:119
msgid "Most Nix commands accept the following command-line options:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:121
msgid "<span id=\"opt-help\">[`--help`](#opt-help)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:123
msgid "Prints out a summary of the command syntax and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:125
msgid "<span id=\"opt-version\">[`--version`](#opt-version)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:127
msgid "Prints out the Nix version number on standard output and exits."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:129
msgid ""
"For machine-readable output, including versions of the libraries Nix links "
"against, see the [`nix version`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-version.md) "
"command."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:132
msgid "<span id=\"opt-verbose\">[`--verbose`](#opt-verbose)</span> / `-v`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:134
msgid ""
"Increases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. For each Nix operation, the information printed on standard output is "
"well-defined; any diagnostic information is printed on standard error, never "
"on standard output."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:138
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. Currently, the following verbosity "
"levels exist:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:141
msgid "`0` “Errors only”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:143
msgid "Only print messages explaining why the Nix invocation failed."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:145
msgid "`1` “Informational”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:147
msgid "Print _useful_ messages about what Nix is doing. This is the default."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:150
msgid "`2` “Talkative”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:152
msgid "Print more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:154
msgid "`3` “Chatty”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:156
msgid "Print even more informational messages."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:158
msgid "`4` “Debug”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:160
msgid "Print debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:162
msgid "`5` “Vomit”"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:164
msgid "Print vast amounts of debug information."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:166
msgid "<span id=\"opt-quiet\">[`--quiet`](#opt-quiet)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:168
msgid ""
"Decreases the level of verbosity of diagnostic messages printed on standard "
"error. This is the inverse option to `-v` / `--verbose`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:171
msgid ""
"This option may be specified repeatedly. See the previous verbosity levels "
"list."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:174
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-log-format\">[`--log-format`](#opt-log-format)</span> _format_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:176
msgid ""
"This option can be used to change the output of the log format, with "
"_format_ being one of:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:178
msgid "`raw`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:180
msgid "This is the raw format, as outputted by nix-build."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:182
msgid "`internal-json`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:184
msgid "Outputs the logs in a structured manner."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:186
msgid "**Warning**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:188
msgid ""
"While the schema itself is relatively stable, the format of the error-"
"messages (namely of the `msg`\\-field) can change between releases."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:192
msgid "`bar`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:194
msgid "Only display a progress bar during the builds."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:196
msgid "`bar-with-logs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:198
msgid "Display the raw logs, with the progress bar at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:200
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-no-build-output\">[`--no-build-output`](#opt-no-build-"
"output)</span> / `-Q`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:202
msgid ""
"By default, output written by builders to standard output and standard error "
"is echoed to the Nix command's standard error. This option suppresses this "
"behaviour. Note that the builder's standard output and error are always "
"written to a log file in `prefix/nix/var/log/nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:206
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-jobs\">[`--max-jobs`](#opt-max-jobs)</span> / `-j` "
"_number_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:208
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of build jobs that Nix will perform in parallel to "
"the specified number. Specify `auto` to use the number of CPUs in the "
"system. The default is specified by the `max-jobs` configuration setting, "
"which itself defaults to `1`. A higher value is useful on SMP systems or to "
"exploit I/O latency."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:213
msgid ""
"Setting it to `0` disallows building on the local machine, which is useful "
"when you want builds to happen only on remote builders."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:215
msgid "<span id=\"opt-cores\">[`--cores`](#opt-cores)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:217
msgid ""
"Sets the value of the `NIX_BUILD_CORES` environment variable in the "
"invocation of builders. Builders can use this variable at their discretion "
"to control the maximum amount of parallelism. For instance, in Nixpkgs, if "
"the derivation attribute `enableParallelBuilding` is set to `true`, the "
"builder passes the `-jN` flag to GNU Make. It defaults to the value of the "
"`cores` configuration setting, if set, or `1` otherwise. The value `0` means "
"that the builder should use all available CPU cores in the system."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:223
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-max-silent-time\">[`--max-silent-time`](#opt-max-silent-"
"time)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:225
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can go without producing "
"any data on standard output or standard error. The default is specified by "
"the `max-silent-time` configuration setting. `0` means no time-out."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:229
msgid "<span id=\"opt-timeout\">[`--timeout`](#opt-timeout)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:231
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum number of seconds that a builder can run. The default is "
"specified by the `timeout` configuration setting. `0` means no timeout."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:235
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-going\">[`--keep-going`](#opt-keep-going)</span> / `-k`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:237
msgid ""
"Keep going in case of failed builds, to the greatest extent possible. That "
"is, if building an input of some derivation fails, Nix will still build the "
"other inputs, but not the derivation itself. Without this option, Nix stops "
"if any build fails (except for builds of substitutes), possibly killing "
"builds in progress (in case of parallel or distributed builds)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:241
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-keep-failed\">[`--keep-failed`](#opt-keep-failed)</span> / `-"
"K`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:243
msgid ""
"Specifies that in case of a build failure, the temporary directory (usually "
"in `/tmp`) in which the build takes place should not be deleted. The path of "
"the build directory is printed as an informational message."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:246
msgid "<span id=\"opt-fallback\">[`--fallback`](#opt-fallback)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:248
msgid ""
"Whenever Nix attempts to build a derivation for which substitutes are known "
"for each output path, but realising the output paths through the substitutes "
"fails, fall back on building the derivation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:250
msgid ""
"The most common scenario in which this is useful is when we have registered "
"substitutes in order to perform binary distribution from, say, a network "
"repository. If the repository is down, the realisation of the derivation "
"will fail. When this option is specified, Nix will build the derivation "
"instead. Thus, installation from binaries falls back on installation from "
"source. This option is not the default since it is generally not desirable "
"for a transient failure in obtaining the substitutes to lead to a full build "
"from source (with the related consumption of resources)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:256
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-readonly-mode\">[`--readonly-mode`](#opt-readonly-mode)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:258
msgid ""
"When this option is used, no attempt is made to open the Nix database. Most "
"Nix operations do need database access, so those operations will fail."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:261
msgid "<span id=\"opt-arg\">[`--arg`](#opt-arg)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:263
msgid ""
"This option is accepted by `nix-env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-shell` and "
"`nix-build`. When evaluating Nix expressions, the expression evaluator will "
"automatically try to call functions that it encounters. It can automatically "
"call functions for which every argument has a [default value](../language/"
"syntax.md#functions) (e.g., `{ argName ?  defaultValue }: ...`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:267
msgid ""
"With `--arg`, you can also call functions that have arguments without a "
"default value (or override a default value). That is, if the evaluator "
"encounters a function with an argument named _name_, it will call it with "
"value _value_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:270
msgid ""
"For instance, the top-level `default.nix` in Nixpkgs is actually a function:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:279
msgid ""
"So if you call this Nix expression (e.g., when you do `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname`), the function will be called automatically using the value "
"[`builtins.currentSystem`](../language/builtins.md) for the `system` "
"argument. You can override this using `--arg`, e.g., `nix-env --install --"
"attr pkgname --arg system \\\"i686-freebsd\\\"`. (Note that since the "
"argument is a Nix string literal, you have to escape the quotes.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:283
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-file\">[`--arg-from-file`](#opt-arg-from-file)</"
"span> _name_ _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:285
msgid ""
"Pass the contents of file _path_ as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:287
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-arg-from-stdin\">[`--arg-from-stdin`](#opt-arg-from-stdin)</"
"span> _name_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:289
msgid "Pass the contents of stdin as the argument _name_ to Nix functions."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:291
msgid "<span id=\"opt-argstr\">[`--argstr`](#opt-argstr)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:293
msgid ""
"This option is like `--arg`, only the value is not a Nix expression but a "
"string. So instead of `--arg system \\\"i686-linux\\\"` (the outer quotes "
"are to keep the shell happy) you can say `--argstr system i686-linux`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:296
msgid "<span id=\"opt-attr\">[`--attr`](#opt-attr)</span> / `-A` _attrPath_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:298
msgid ""
"Select an attribute from the top-level Nix expression being evaluated. (`nix-"
"env`, `nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.) The _attribute "
"path_ _attrPath_ is a sequence of attribute names separated by dots. For "
"instance, given a top-level Nix expression _e_, the attribute path `xorg."
"xorgserver` would cause the expression `e.xorg.xorgserver` to be used. See "
"[`nix-env --install`](../command-ref/nix-env/install.md) for some concrete "
"examples."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:304
msgid ""
"In addition to attribute names, you can also specify array indices. For "
"instance, the attribute path `foo.3.bar` selects the `bar` attribute of the "
"fourth element of the array in the `foo` attribute of the top-level "
"expression."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:309
msgid ""
"<span id=\"opt-eval-store\">[`--eval-store`](#opt-eval-store)</span> _store-"
"url_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:311
msgid ""
"The [URL to the Nix store](../store/types/index.md#store-url-format) to use "
"for evaluation, i.e. where to store derivations (`.drv` files) and inputs "
"referenced by them."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:313
msgid "<span id=\"opt-expr\">[`--expr`](#opt-expr)</span> / `-E`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:315
msgid ""
"Interpret the command line arguments as a list of Nix expressions to be "
"parsed and evaluated, rather than as a list of file names of Nix "
"expressions. (`nix-instantiate`, `nix-build` and `nix-shell` only.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:318
msgid ""
"For `nix-shell`, this option is commonly used to give you a shell in which "
"you can build the packages returned by the expression. If you want to get a "
"shell which contain the _built_ packages ready for use, give your expression "
"to the `nix-shell --packages ` convenience flag instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:321
msgid "<span id=\"opt-I\">[`-I` / `--include`](#opt-I)</span> _path_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:323
msgid ""
"Add an entry to the list of search paths used to resolve [lookup paths](../"
"language/constructs/lookup-path.md). This option may be given multiple times."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:326
msgid ""
"Paths added through `-I` take precedence over the [`nix-path` configuration "
"setting](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-nix-path) and the [`NIX_PATH` "
"environment variable](../command-ref/env-common.md#env-NIX_PATH)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:328
msgid "<span id=\"opt-impure\">[`--impure`](#opt-impure)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:330
msgid "Allow access to mutable paths and repositories."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:332
msgid "<span id=\"opt-option\">[`--option`](#opt-option)</span> _name_ _value_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:334
msgid ""
"Set the Nix configuration option _name_ to _value_. This overrides settings "
"in the Nix configuration file (see nix.conf5)."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:337
msgid "<span id=\"opt-repair\">[`--repair`](#opt-repair)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:339
msgid ""
"Fix corrupted or missing store paths by redownloading or rebuilding them. "
"Note that this is slow because it requires computing a cryptographic hash of "
"the contents of every path in the closure of the build. Also note the "
"warning under `nix-store --repair-path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:343 source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:355
#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:707
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:345
msgid ""
"See [`man nix.conf`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#command-line-flags) for "
"overriding configuration settings with command line flags."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:348
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:350
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_BUILD_SHELL\">[`NIX_BUILD_SHELL`](#env-NIX_BUILD_SHELL)</"
"span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:352
msgid ""
"Shell used to start the interactive environment. Defaults to the `bash` from "
"`bashInteractive` found in `<nixpkgs>`, falling back to the `bash` found in "
"`PATH` if not found."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:357
msgid ""
"The shell obtained using this method may not necessarily be the same as any "
"shells requested in _path_."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:361
msgid "\\*\\*Example"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:363
msgid ""
"Despite `--pure`, this invocation will not result in a fully reproducible "
"shell environment:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:365
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"#!/usr/bin/env -S nix-shell --pure\n"
"let\n"
"  pkgs = import (fetchTarball \"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/"
"archive/854fdc68881791812eddd33b2fed94b954979a8e.tar.gz\") {};\n"
"in\n"
"pkgs.mkShell {\n"
"  buildInputs = pkgs.bashInteractive;\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:375
msgid "Common Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:377
msgid "Most Nix commands interpret the following environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:379
msgid "Configuration environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:381
msgid ""
"The following environment variables affect how Nix loads its configuration. "
"See the [configuration file](../command-ref/conf-file.md#configuration-file) "
"documentation for full details."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:384
msgid ""
"<span id=\"env-NIX_CONF_DIR\">[`NIX_CONF_DIR`](#env-NIX_CONF_DIR)</span>"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:386
msgid "Overrides the system configuration directory."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-shell.md:388
msgid ""
